From b4729b678d50252befb10eae00f6a617814e213d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rain Valentine <rsg000@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 23:29:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] kvstore: check the lane memory partition at run time
 (STAGED_CHECKS)

While a kvstore is in concurrent mode (a WRITE, APPLY or MAINT phase), every
access to one of its tables goes through kvstoreGetHashtable or its Ref
variant, which now asserts that the calling thread claimed that table for the
phase: a write or apply lane claims every table with didx % nlanes == lane
(fastpathStagedWriteLane, the replica plan and apply lanes), a MAINT unit
claims its one table. Main while it waits at the barrier, an IO thread's inbox
job, or a lane reaching a key outside its partition all fail the check. This
is obligation O5 of the proof (the per-partition tables are a memory
partition) checked on every table access instead of assumed.

The empty-window flag now closes at the end of the two batch executors
instead of in writePhase, so the unit-test harnesses that drive the halves
themselves close it too. The kvstore unit tests that play a lane on the test
thread claim the tables they touch. The unit Makefile passes STAGED_CHECKS to
the C++ side for that.

Signed-off-by: Rain Valentine <rsg000@gmail.com>
